{"name":"French Marron","hex":"#ad747d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"french","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare food by cutting it into strips.","To kiss (another person) while inserting one’s tongue into the other person's mouth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/french"},{"term":"marron","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet chestnut. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Cherax tenuimanus, a species of freshwater crayfish from Western Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marron","blocks":[{"text":"Marron is a name given to two closely related species of crayfish in Western Australia. Formerly considered a single species, it is since recognised as comprising two species, the critically endangered Cherax tenuimanus, and the species that is outcompeting it, C. cainii."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Cooked_Marron_KI_2008.JPG/330px-Cooked_Marron_KI_2008.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marron"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"french":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fb/En-us-French.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fb/En-us-French.ogg/En-us-French.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bc/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-french.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/bc/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-french.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-french.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c